10:43:38.457 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] ## Why This Solves the Problems
10:43:38.458 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] 
10:43:38.458 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] The issues occurred because Diffblue Cover was trying to test these methods and needed to create TAQWriter instances. When it used File-based constructors, temporary files were created but not cleaned up within the test execution.
10:43:38.459 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] 
10:43:38.459 [INFO]   [Reporting]   [main]              [com.diffblue.cover.ui.controller.aa] [Claude Code] By providing `@InterestingTestFactory` annotated methods that use in-memory streams (`ByteArrayOutputStream`), Cover will now prefer these factories over direct File constructor calls. This eliminates the need for temporary files altogether during testing of these methods, satisfying Cover's R020 requirement that temporary files must be deleted.
